WEBVTT

cue-1
00:00:00.539 --> 00:00:07.159
Ah, allow me to introduce myself. I am the
New Interests' election agent,

cue-2
00:00:07.159 --> 00:00:12.479
managing this whole campaign. May I
inquire how you will be voting in the

cue-3
00:00:12.479 --> 00:00:18.140
coming poll? Shall I write your name in my
book? See, I'm putting sure votes on the

cue-4
00:00:18.140 --> 00:00:24.340
left. And yes, true, no names so far, so
perhaps I should put you down among the

cue-5
00:00:24.340 --> 00:00:30.180
doubtful votes on the right? In truth, it
makes me wonder whether all this treating

cue-6
00:00:30.180 --> 00:00:36.279
will have been worth it. But we shall know
on polling day. Voting, as you'll know,

cue-7
00:00:36.279 --> 00:00:41.979
is done openly, so we shall see soon
enough whether or not these people thank

cue-8
00:00:41.979 --> 00:00:48.380
us for our hospitality with their votes.
If they don't, they'll be sure to regret

cue-9
00:00:48.380 --> 00:00:55.259
it. Look. See how those Old Interests
dupes parade outside the

cue-10
00:00:55.259 --> 00:01:02.119
window? Ridiculous! They protest against
even the most moderate new laws. We

cue-11
00:01:02.119 --> 00:01:07.040
passed the Marriage Act this year, and the
Jewish Naturalization Act the year

cue-12
00:01:07.040 --> 00:01:12.479
before, the most moderate of measures. But
these stuck-in-the-past fools have been

cue-13
00:01:12.479 --> 00:01:18.579
rioting about them for months. I see
they're trying to break the door down.

cue-14
00:01:18.580 --> 00:01:25.479
They won't get in. Don't worry. There's no
threat to us in here. Ow!

cue-15
00:01:25.479 --> 00:01:28.199
Who threw that brick?
